```python
def most_common_char(s):
    counts = {}
    for ch in s:
        counts[ch] = counts.get(ch, 0) + 1
    max_count = max(counts.values())
    most_common = [ch for ch, count in counts.items() if count == max_count]
    return most_common[0]
```

Please note that this function will return any character that appears most frequently in the string, in case of a tie. If you want to return all characters that appear most frequently, you can modify the function to return `most_common` instead of `most_common[0]`.
